  "description": "Illustrious-based checkpoint by LatteLeopard (civitai.com/models/1261882), trained across a mixed Danbooru/e621/Rule34 tag set with a wide style range (furry/kemono through anime and western toon) rather than furry-only. The creator documents v3.0+ as 'Euler A sampler only' and cfg 4 as the 'go-to' value (4-7 usable range, 20+ steps) — those, plus clip_skip -2 and the quality-tag convention below, mirror furrytoonmix_illustrious.json's own verified NoobAI/Illustrious-family values since this is the same base architecture, but are otherwise a community-recommended starting point, not tuned against a specific install. tag_dictionary is left unset (searches/checks both dictionaries) since the model explicitly blends Danbooru and e621/Rule34 tags rather than favoring one. loras starts empty deliberately — civitai_base_models below opts this profile into lora_discovery.py's propagation pass, which backfills any Illustrious LoRA furrytoonmix_illustrious.json (or any other opted-in profile) already has a cached CivitAI lookup for, disabled by default, on the next boot or /reload; anything never looked up at all (a hand-typed entry that predates any Info tap or discovery run) still needs a manual /lora Info tap or a manual loras entry first.",
